  - For rows with arxiv_id: fetch export.arxiv.org/api/query?id_list=<id>; parse entry: title, authors, published, updated, summary, journal_ref, comment, doi.
  - For rows without arxiv: fetch api.crossref.org/works/<doi>; parse title, authors, year (issued), container-title, volume, page, type.
  - For rows with both, fetch both (primary = arXiv for title/authors/excerpt; Crossref for venue/year journal).
- Comparisons:
  - title: normalized exact/prefix/similarity.
  - authors: first-author surname + count.
  - year: ledger year vs fetched (allow ±1 for issue/online conventions) — like 086.
  - venue: tokens.
  - excerpt: similarity of ledger evidence_excerpt to fetched abstract (first 400 chars; use difflib SequenceMatcher ratio, but note quotes are topical summaries not verbatim abstracts — 086 reported excerpt mismatch everywhere; I'll record similarity but not treat excerpt mismatch as hard failure by itself; record as a "quote_not_verbatim" note).
- Verdict rules (declared before fetch):
  - FETCH_FAILED if all fetches fail.
  - MISMATCH if title mismatch (neither exact after normalization nor fetched title is a prefix of ledger title or vice versa) or first-author surname absent, or year differs by >1.
  - PARTIAL if title/author/year agree but locator quality issues (search-query locator rather than exact), or year convention off-by-one, or venue unverifiable.
  - MATCH if title exact, author match, year exact/±1 with venue match.
- Also record locator_kind: exact (arxiv abs/doi URL) vs search_query vs other.

The script should be deterministic and stdlib-only, cache raw fetch bodies in `raw/` with sha256. Since network live, the raw bodies prove fetch.

